## Scenarios

### tail tool

#### line selection

#### gets last N lines

- Verify: gets last N lines
   - Expected: result equals `line3\nline4\nline5`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: gets last N lines")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val content = "line1\nline2\nline3\nline4\nline5"
val result = tail_lines(content, 3)
expect(result).to_equal("line3\nline4\nline5")
```

</details>

#### returns all lines when N exceeds count

- Verify: returns all lines when N exceeds count
   - Expected: result equals `line1\nline2`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: returns all lines when N exceeds count")
val content = "line1\nline2"
val result = tail_lines(content, 10)
expect(result).to_equal("line1\nline2")
```

</details>

#### returns last line

- Verify: returns last line
   - Expected: result equals `last`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: returns last line")
val content = "first\nlast"
val result = tail_lines(content, 1)
expect(result).to_equal("last")
```

</details>

